# Veggie Loaded Red Curry

Based on [https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/…](https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/veggie-loaded-red-curry/17022) (wayback unavailable) (wayback unavailable)

{ rating="3" image="veggie_loaded_red_curry.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1/2 medium [sweet onion]{ ing="sweet-onion" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 large [red bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }, seeded and thinly sliced
- [ ] 1/2 small [cauliflower head]{ ing="cauliflower-head" }, cut into florets (2 cups)
- [ ] ~2 Tbsp [pure sesame oil]{ ing="pure-sesame-oil" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [mild red curry paste]{ ing="mild-red-curry-paste" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ginger]{ ing="ginger" } (or 1-inch piece peeled fresh ginger root, grated)
- [ ] 8 oz (2 cups) [frozen cubed butternut squash]{ ing="frozen-cubed-butternut-squash" } (or frozen cubed sweet potatoes)
- [ ] 1 cup [full-fat coconut milk]{ ing="full-fat-coconut-milk" } (see Note)
- [ ] 1 cup [low-sodium vegetable broth]{ ing="low-sodium-vegetable-broth" }
- [ ] One 15-oz [can crushed tomatoes]{ ing="can-crushed-tomatoes" } (or tomato sauce or can of diced tomatoes)
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] (Optional) 1 [Fresno pepper]{ ing="fresno-pepper" }, seeded and thinly sliced
- [ ] 2 oz [baby spinach leaves]{ ing="baby-spinach-leaves" } (2 cups)
- [ ] 3 cups [cooked white]{ ing="cooked-white" } or brown long-grain rice
- [ ] 1 [lime]{ ing="lime" }, cut into wedges, for serving

## Recipe

1. Chop the [onion]{ ing="sweet-onion" } and [bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" } (thin slice) and cauliflower (florets)
1. Heat [oil]{ ing="pure-sesame-oil" } in a large pot over medium heat. Add the [onion]{ ing="sweet-onion" }, red [curry paste]{ ing="mild-red-curry-paste" }, and [ginger]{ ing="ginger" }. Cook for 5 minutes until the onion has softened
1. Add the [red bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }, cauliflower, frozen [butternut squash]{ ing="frozen-cubed-butternut-squash" } (or sweet potatoes), [coconut milk]{ ing="full-fat-coconut-milk" }, [broth]{ ing="low-sodium-vegetable-broth" }, canned [tomatoes]{ ing="can-crushed-tomatoes" }, and [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
1. Cook, gently bubbling at the edges, for 13 minutes
1. Add the spinach (and if using, [Fresno pepper]{ ing="fresno-pepper" }). Cook for 2 minutes
1. Serve warm over rice, with a few squeezes of [lime]{ ing="lime" }

## Notes

1. **Note: Thoroughly stir the coconut milk before using, to re-incorporate its fat. You’ll also use most of the remaining coconut milk from a 15-oz can in the Green Chile Mac recipe
1. If adding carrots, add in when cooking the onions and sauce
1. Week 3

### Recipe Philosophy

- **Balanced coconut approach:** Uses only 1 cup (half can) full-fat coconut milk to avoid overpowering flavor - compare to similar curries that use full 14oz cans
- **Red curry paste shortcut:** 3 Tbsp curry paste provides complex flavor without measuring individual spices or tempering
